IMPORT prelude

-- Statutory Boards (Taxable Services) Act 1968 (Singapore) -- who counts as a statutory board (s 2), which services are taxable and
-- who pays (s 3(1), (4), s 6), the 50% additional tax on electricity for specified commercial buildings and who bears it (s 3(2),
-- (3)), recovery fees and late-payment charges (s 3(2A)), the validation of earlier late-payment charges (s 4A), collection and
-- recovery by the board (s 4) and where the money goes (s 5).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1 April 2024), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SBTSA1968.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021";
-- the latest amendment annotated is Act 4 of 2008 (Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008), annotated "wef 01/04/2024" on
-- s 3(2A) and s 4A, and listed in the Legislative History with commencement 1 April 2024. The arrangement of sections at the top of
-- the deposit is shifted by one line against the headings; the body's numbering (1, 2, 3, 4, 4A, 5, 6, 7) is followed here.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0150 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet. The
-- whole operative Act (ss 2 to 6) is encoded; it is short. Not encoded: the rate of any tax, which the Act leaves to Gazette orders
-- (none was retrieved), the Minister's rule-making power (s 7), the duty to present orders to Parliament (s 3(5)), and the content
-- of the "written law relating to the recovery of any fees" that s 4(2) borrows.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Statutory Boards (Taxable Services) Act 1968 -- tax on services`

§§ `2 -- statutory board`

-- s 2: "statutory board" INCLUDES "a public telecommunication licensee referred to in the Telecommunications Act 1999, a gas licensee
-- under the Gas Act 2001 and a market support services licensee under the Electricity Act 2001". "services" includes "the letting of
-- any apparatus or appliance". "taxable services" means the services of a statutory board specified to be taxable under section 3.
-- The word "includes" means private licensees are statutory boards for this Act; a company holding none of those licences is not
-- (the Act gives no other definition, so an ordinary statutory board is taken to be one set up by statute -- an inference).
DECLARE Supplier IS ONE OF
    `a statutory board set up by statute`
    `a public telecommunication licensee`
    `a gas licensee`
    `a market support services licensee`
    `a company holding none of those licences`

GIVEN `the supplier` IS A Supplier
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplier counts as a statutory board` IF
    CONSIDER `the supplier`
    WHEN `a company holding none of those licences` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3(1), (4) and 6 -- taxable services and who pays`

-- s 3(1): the Minister may, "by order published in the Gazette", specify services rendered by any statutory board to be taxable
-- services, "and may in such order prescribe the rate of tax".
-- s 3(4): "any services in respect of which fees or other charges are collected by a statutory board on behalf of the Government
-- shall be deemed to be services rendered by that statutory board".
-- s 4(1): the board collects "any tax payable by any person to whom the taxable services have been rendered".
-- s 6: "The Minister may, by order, exempt any person or class of persons from the payment of any tax under this Act."
DECLARE Service HAS
    `the supplier` IS A Supplier
    `rendered by the supplier itself` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fees collected by the supplier on behalf of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
    `specified as taxable by a Gazette order` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the service` IS A Service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is a taxable service` IF
        `the supplier counts as a statutory board` (`the service`'s `the supplier`)
    AND (    `the service`'s `rendered by the supplier itself`
         OR  `the service`'s `fees collected by the supplier on behalf of the Government`)
    AND `the service`'s `specified as taxable by a Gazette order`

GIVEN `the service` IS A Service, `the person received the service` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person is exempted by Minister's order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person must pay the tax` IF
        `the service is a taxable service` `the service`
    AND `the person received the service`
    AND (NOT `the person is exempted by Minister's order`)

-- The Act fixes no rate for the tax itself; the order prescribes it. The amount is the charge times the order's rate.
GIVEN `the service` IS A Service, `the charges` IS A NUMBER, `the order's rate in percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax on the service` MEANS
    IF `the service is a taxable service` `the service`
    THEN `the charges` TIMES `the order's rate in percent` DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE 0

§§ `3(2), (3) -- additional tax on electricity for commercial buildings`

-- s 3(2): an order "may prescribe an additional tax at the rate of 50% of the charges for any electrical energy supplied to such
-- commercial buildings or class of commercial buildings as may be specified in the order and any additional tax so prescribed shall be
-- paid by the owners of such buildings".
-- s 3(3): "owners" has the same meaning as in the Property Tax Act 1960; and "a reference to a commercial building is deemed to
-- include any part of the building which is used for residential purposes".
-- The rate here is fixed by the Act at 50%: the order chooses only whether to impose it and on which buildings.
GIVEN `the electricity charges` IS A NUMBER, `an order prescribes the additional tax` IS A BOOLEAN, `the building is specified in the order` IS A BOOLEAN, `the supply is to a part used for residential purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the additional tax` MEANS
    IF `an order prescribes the additional tax` AND `the building is specified in the order`
    THEN `the electricity charges` TIMES 50 DIVIDED BY 100
    ELSE 0

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF
    `the owner of the building`
    `a tenant occupying the building`
    `a resident of a flat in the building`
    `the statutory board supplying the electricity`

GIVEN `the party` IS A Party
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the party must pay the additional tax` IF
    CONSIDER `the party`
    WHEN `the owner of the building` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3(2A) and 4A -- recovery fees and late-payment charges`

-- s 3(2A) [Act 4 of 2008 wef 01/04/2024]: an order may prescribe "(a) the fees and costs payable for the recovery of any tax or
-- additional tax, whether by instalment or otherwise; and (b) the charges payable for the late payment of any tax or additional tax".
-- s 4A [same]: "Every amount collected, on behalf of the Government, before the date of commencement of the Statutes (Miscellaneous
-- Amendments) Act 2008 as, or purportedly as, a charge for the late payment of any tax or additional tax shall be deemed to be and
-- always to have been validly collected, and no legal proceedings shall lie or be instituted or maintained in any court of law".
-- The Legislative History gives the 2008 Act's commencement as 1 April 2024, which is the date used here.
-- Dates are written as year, month and day.
GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the date code` MEANS `y` TIMES 10000 PLUS `m` TIMES 100 PLUS `d`

GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER, `the order prescribes late-payment charges` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3(2A) authorises a late-payment charge` IF
        `the date code` `y` `m` `d` AT LEAST 20240401
    AND `the order prescribes late-payment charges`

GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER, `collected as a late-payment charge` IS A BOOLEAN, `collected on behalf of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4A validates the collection` IF
        `the date code` `y` `m` `d` LESS THAN 20240401
    AND `collected as a late-payment charge`
    AND `collected on behalf of the Government`

GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER, `collected as a late-payment charge` IS A BOOLEAN, `collected on behalf of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4A bars a claim to get the charge back` IF
    `section 4A validates the collection` `y` `m` `d` `collected as a late-payment charge` `collected on behalf of the Government`

§§ `4 and 5 -- collection, recovery and the Consolidated Fund`

-- s 4(1): "the appropriate statutory board shall assess and collect, on behalf of the Government," the tax and any additional tax,
-- "in such manner as that statutory board may, with the approval of the Minister, determine".
-- s 4(2): to recover tax the board may, "subject to any rules made under this Act", exercise its powers under any written law for the
-- recovery of its own fees or charges.
-- s 5: "All tax collected by a statutory board under this Act shall be paid into the Consolidated Fund."
DECLARE Destination IS ONE OF
    `the Consolidated Fund`
    `the statutory board's own funds`

GIVETH A Destination
`where collected tax goes` MEANS `the Consolidated Fund`

GIVEN `the manner of collection has the Minister's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board's manner of collection is authorised` IF `the manner of collection has the Minister's approval`

GIVEN `rules under the Act restrict the power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board may use its own fee-recovery powers for the tax` IF NOT `rules under the Act restrict the power`
